    "input": "search_document: Hello Sarah,\n\nThank you for reaching out to Northwind Outdoor Support. I understand your concerns regarding the fees applied to your recent return. I have reviewed your questions against our current policies to provide you with the accurate information.\n\n**Regarding the $12.50 Prepaid Return Label Fee**\nThe charge you are seeing is consistent with our policy. Standard ground shipping costs for returns are the customer\u2019s responsibility. We offer a prepaid return label for a flat fee of $12.50 [returns]. This fee covers the cost of the label and the standard shipping service. If you had chosen to ship via an expedited carrier, you would have been responsible for the full shipping cost upfront, with only the standard rate reimbursed upon receipt [returns]. Therefore, the $12.50 charge is the standard, non-refundable cost for using our prepaid label service.\n\n**Regarding the 15% Restocking Fee**\nAccording to our policy, a 15% restocking fee is deducted **only** if the item shows signs of wear, dirt, or damage, or if it is not in its original, unused condition with all tags, manuals, and protective packaging intact [returns]. You stated that your tent was in perfect, unused condition, in original packaging, with all tags attached, and never opened or used.\n\nBased on the policy excerpt provided, if the item met these specific conditions (original, unused, tags/packaging intact), the restocking fee should **not** have been applied. The fee is specifically for items that fail to meet this \"perfect condition\" standard [returns].\n\n**Next Steps**\nSince the policy states the fee is conditional on the item's condition, and you confirm the item was in perfect condition, I recommend we escalate this ticket to a human agent. They can review the specific inspection notes from our warehouse staff to verify if the item was indeed flagged for wear/damage or if there was an error in applying the fee.\n\nPlease note that I cannot directly modify your account or remove fees myself, as I must rely strictly on the handbook policies and cannot access your specific order inspection records. However, based on the policy, if the item was truly in perfect condition, the fee appears to be incorrectly applied.\n\nWould you like me to escalate this ticket to a human agent for a detailed review of your inspection report and potential fee reversal?\n\n[returns]",
    "model": "nomic-embed-text",
